@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB Customer Entitlement Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki customer entitlement integration to osb works properly.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the contact entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| Liferay Role    |
	| NonLiferay Role |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Role    |
	| NonLiferay Account Role |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay OSB Product |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from the support organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from the support organization "Koroneiki NonLiferay Role"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the organizations with the following names from customer.liferay.com
	| Koroneiki Liferay Role    |
	| Koroneiki NonLiferay Role |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Sync user and organization via Koroneiki
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Koroneiki customer contacts with the proper entitlements synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to OSB if the OSB site contains the appropriate organization.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "KORONEKORONE" should be part of the support site
	When I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                         |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay OSB Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "A Liferay OSB Product" and contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role" and type "Account Customer" with the following values
	| Description | Liferay Role Entitlement |
	| Name        | Liferay Role             |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create a support organization with the name "Koroneiki Liferay Role"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Role"
	Then the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member
	And the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should not have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member

Scenario: Sync updated users via Koroneiki role change
	New and removed koroneiki customer contacts with the proper entitlements synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to OSB if the OSB site contains the appropriate organization.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "KORONEKORONE" should be part of the support site
	When I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                         |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay OSB Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "A Liferay OSB Product" and contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role" and type "Account Customer" with the following values
	| Description | Liferay Role Entitlement |
	| Name        | Liferay Role             |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create a support organization with the name "Koroneiki Liferay Role"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Role"
	Then the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member
	And the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should not have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member
	When I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from the following roles	
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| NonLiferay Account Role |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Role"
	Then the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member
	And the organization "Koroneiki Liferay Role" should not have the user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a member

Scenario: Sync updated users via Koroneiki product purchase removal
	Koroneiki product purchase removal followed by an entitlement sync should properly sync to OSB if the OSB site contains the appropriate organization.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
